comments.body:
Confirmed. I own the log-log MAE figure and table material under `report/figures/` per the published assignment (7ee717e), and I confirm the proposed filename. Delivering:

- `report/figures/error_scaling.svg` (primary) and `report/figures/error_scaling.png` — log-log mean absolute error vs N for 10^3..10^7 with decade tick labels, the OLS fitted line annotated with the exponent and both 95% intervals (paired-run bootstrap as primary, OLS-t with 3 df as diagnostic, since review wants both in the report), the -1/2 asymptotic benchmark line, and a band showing the 2.5-97.5% range of the 200 run errors at each N.
- `report/figures/error_table.md` — the five-row table (N as powers of 10, MAE, per-N SE, MAE/benchmark ratio), the fitted exponent with both intervals, and the figure caption, formatted for direct inclusion in `report/report.md`.
- `report/figures/make_figure.py` + `report/figures/PROVENANCE.md` — generator and provenance so the figure and table regenerate from your committed result files.

I plot and tabulate exactly your committed numbers; nothing is recomputed on my side (the fitted line is rendered from your committed intercept/slope at your committed N, and the benchmark curve from your committed benchmark values). The machine-readable schema my generator expects is pinned in `work/make_figure.py` at commit 3488a91; the required JSON keys are:

1. `N`, `mae` — the five sample sizes and five mean absolute errors;
2. `run_error_p025`, `run_error_p975` — per-N 2.5th/97.5th percentiles of the 200 per-run absolute errors (for the spread band);
3. `mae_se`, `benchmark_mae` — the per-N standard errors and analytic asymptotic benchmark MAE values you already record for the review checks (so the benchmark line and ratio column are your committed values);
4. `ols` with `intercept`, `slope`, and `t_interval_95`; `bootstrap` with `interval_95`, `replicates`, `seed` (plus the second-seed stability interval if available);
5. `provenance` with the seed convention and versions.

A per-run errors file (200 x 5) is welcome for the record but not needed for the figure. My figure and table work starts once that results file is pushed; the split and paths are otherwise settled as proposed.
